    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Read draft structure information as JSON (read-only).\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference to inspect\r\n          --dir TEXT          Optional parent directory for resolving the draft project folder.\r\n          --scope <full|summary|timeline|attribute|identify|layout> \r\n                              Information scope to read:\r\n                              full/summary/timeline/attribute/identify/layout\r\n          --seg-id TEXT ...   Raw segment id filter. Repeatable\r\n          --protocol <stdraft> \r\n                              Read protocol. Only stdraft is currently supported; default\r\n                              stdraft\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  summary                     Read a compact draft overview for locating segment ids.\r\n\r\nREAD-ONLY\r\n  This command inspects the draft and prints stdout JSON field `json_result`.\r\n  It does not render media, export files, write patches, or modify the draft.\r\n\r\n  Prefer `draft extract summary` for compact summary reads; the --scope form remains a compatibility path.\r\n\r\nSCOPE (what --scope reads; default full)\r\n  full       Complete draft / segment structure.\r\n  summary    Compact overview for locating stable segment ids.\r\n  timeline   Track order, segment timing, and sequencing information.\r\n  layout     Canvas / spatial layout information.\r\n  attribute  Per-segment attributes and editable properties.\r\n  identify   Identity information such as ids.\r\n\r\nSEGMENT FILTER\r\n  Omit --seg-id to inspect the whole draft. Repeat --seg-id to limit the\r\n  returned structure to specific raw segment ids.\r\n\r\nPROTOCOL\r\n  Only `stdraft` is supported today; it is the default.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Inspect a compact overview to locate stable segment ids\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract summary --ref local://example\r\n  # Read track order and per-segment timing\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract --ref local://example --scope timeline\r\n  # Limit attribute output to specific segments\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract --ref local://example --scope attribute --seg-id id1 --seg-id id2\r\n  # Full structure with the protocol given explicitly (stdraft is the default)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract --ref local://example --scope full --protocol stdraft\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Read draft structure information as JSON (read-only).\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference to inspect\r\n          --dir TEXT          Optional parent directory for resolving the draft project folder.\r\n          --scope <full|summary|timeline|attribute|identify|layout> \r\n                              Information scope to read:\r\n                              full/summary/timeline/attribute/identify/layout\r\n          --seg-id TEXT ...   Raw segment id filter. Repeatable\r\n          --protocol <stdraft> \r\n                              Read protocol. Only stdraft is currently supported; default\r\n                              stdraft\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  summary                     Read a compact draft overview for locating segment ids.\r\n\r\nREAD-ONLY\r\n  This command inspects the draft and prints stdout JSON field `json_result`.\r\n  It does not render media, export files, write patches, or modify the draft.\r\n\r\n  Prefer `draft extract summary` for compact summary reads; the --scope form remains a compatibility path.\r\n\r\nSCOPE (what --scope reads; default full)\r\n  full       Complete draft / segment structure.\r\n  summary    Compact overview for locating stable segment ids.\r\n  timeline   Track order, segment timing, and sequencing information.\r\n  layout     Canvas / spatial layout information.\r\n  attribute  Per-segment attributes and editable properties.\r\n  identify   Identity information such as ids.\r\n\r\nSEGMENT FILTER\r\n  Omit --seg-id to inspect the whole draft. Repeat --seg-id to limit the\r\n  returned structure to specific raw segment ids.\r\n\r\nPROTOCOL\r\n  Only `stdraft` is supported today; it is the default.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Inspect a compact overview to locate stable segment ids\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract summary --ref local://example\r\n  # Read track order and per-segment timing\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract --ref local://example --scope timeline\r\n  # Limit attribute output to specific segments\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract --ref local://example --scope attribute --seg-id id1 --seg-id id2\r\n  # Full structure with the protocol given explicitly (stdraft is the default)\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft extract --ref local://example --scope full --protocol stdraft\r\n",
